# Hacker News @@VERSION@@ — @@KIND@@

Source commit: @@COMMIT@@. Target: Linux/amd64. See manifest.json for source
image tags/IDs and SHA-256 hashes of every payload file (the manifest does not
hash itself). SHA256SUMS in the release covers all seven complete ZIPs.

## Image deployment (Docker Compose v2)

The combined bundle has all six payloads under applications/ and images/;
there are no nested ZIPs. For individual image bundles, extract all three into
one directory (their compose files are identical). Load each included TAR:

```sh
docker load --input images/api.tar
docker load --input images/blazor.tar
docker load --input images/react.tar
docker compose -p hackernews-release -f compose.release.yml up -d --no-build --pull never
```

API: http://localhost:8080/health; React: http://localhost:8081;
Blazor: http://localhost:8082. Stop with
`docker compose -p hackernews-release -f compose.release.yml down`.
Logs persist in the project's api-logs volume; down does not delete it.
No checkout, build context, fixture, Portainer, or registry is required.
This is the production stack: it uses the live Hacker News upstream by default.

Release/default Compose trusts the configured Docker subnet (default
172.30.80.0/24), unlike smoke's single-proxy trust. Keep this subnet private;
only trusted containers should join it. Set HN_DOCKER_SUBNET for collisions.
HN_BASE_URL, HN_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (10), HN_REFRESH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (120),
and HN_BLAZOR_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (130) retain the default stack's semantics.

## Framework-dependent applications (without their images)

Install the .NET 10 **ASP.NET Core runtime** for Linux x64 (not only the base
.NET runtime). No SDK or self-contained executable is included. From the
extracted application directory, run:

```sh
cd applications/api
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production ASPNETCORE_HTTP_PORTS=8080 dotnet HackerNews.BestStories.Api.dll
```

In a second terminal, from the extraction root:

```sh
cd applications/blazor
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production ASPNETCORE_HTTP_PORTS=8082 ApiBaseUrl=http://localhost:8080/ dotnet HackerNews.BestStories.Blazor.dll
```

Keep each publish directory and Blazor wwwroot intact. Give the API a writable
logs directory. Set ApiBaseUrl to the API's address as reachable **from the
Blazor server**, including its trailing slash. Configure trusted proxies
explicitly when deploying the applications behind your own proxy.

## React static application

applications/react/html contains production static assets;
applications/react/nginx/default.conf is the matching nginx/proxy config.
Serve them with nginx at /usr/share/nginx/html and
/etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf respectively. This is not a file:// application.
Its /api proxy expects the Docker DNS name api:8080 on the shared network and
Docker's DNS resolver; outside Docker, adapt DNS/upstream configuration to
your deployment. Prefer the supplied React image/Compose to preserve the
tested policy. The application-only ZIP does not include nginx itself.

Individual application ZIPs contain only the named application's payload.
Their compose file is provided for reference/image deployment and requires
the three separately loaded images; it does not rebuild application files.